H 1000
	\bGAME\B: \h020\ba\Buto\bs\Bave, \ba\Buto\blo\Bad, \bsav\Be, \blo\Bad, \bpl\Bay
	\bBASE\B: \h023\bl\Baunch, \bpa\Brk, \bd\Brive, \bx\Bfer, \bse\Bll, \bhi\Btch
	\bMOVE\B: \h022\bj\Bump, \bpos[r]\B, \brot[r]\B, \bb\Base, \bs\Bystem
	\bSHIP\B: \h028\bcs\Bpd, \bcac\Bc, \ban\Bim, \bgh\Bost, \bgo\Bdmode, \bdrain\B(\bs\Belf/\bt\Bgt), \bkill\B(\bs\Belf/\bt\Bgt)
	\bHUD\B: \h032\bn\Btb, \bsho\Bw, \bz\Boom, (\bun\B)\bma\Brk
	\bPLAYER\B: \bcas\Bh, \bre\Bp, \bshi\Bps, \bmo\Bnkey, \brob\Bot, \bt\Brent, \bcos\Btume
    \bMISC\B: \h026\bcom\Bmands, \bcoi\Bn, \bdi\Bce, \bpi\Bng, \bpr\Bint/\bsay\B, \bti\Bme

	Enter \bhelp \itopic\B\I  for further help.

	Commands (and their options) can be abbreviated to a unique prefix. Case is ignored, unless otherwise stated. Commands that search for names will stop at the first match found; \
	append \b*\B, \b**\B or \b*\iN\B\I  to stop at the second, third or \iN \Ith match.\.

H 1001
	\bautosave\B\h081save the Auto Save game
	\bautoload\B\h085load the Auto Save game
	\bsave [\islot \I|\idesc \I]\B\h020save the game
	\bload [\islot \I|\idesc \I]\B\h024load a game
	\bplay \isound \I [\iutf \I]\B\h062play a sound effect

	Only \bsave\Bd games can be \bload\Bed. Slot is a single character and will be listed as "Quick Save \islot\I "; it is converted to upper case and appended to the file name, so \
	not all characters are available. Described games will be listed with a leading space. Games are automatically overwritten.\.

H 1002
	\blaunch\B\h063enter space
	\bpark\B\h082place the ship in storage
	\bdrive [\iship \I]\B\h025get a ship out of storage
	\bxfer [\iship \I]\B\h035transfer equipment and commodities
	\bsell [\iship \I]\B\h037sell a ship in storage
	\bhitch [\ibase \I]\B\h020hitch a ride

	\iShip  \Iis tested as a prefix of the name. It is optional (except for \bsell\B) if there is only one ship stored on the base, otherwise the ships will be listed. \iBase  \Imay \
	only be omitted if you have ships stored on one other base.\.

H 1003
	\bjump \iz, x, y\B\I\h112move forwards/backwards, right/left, up/down
	\bjump [\iobject\I ]\B\h096move to the (targeted) object
	\bpos [=]\in\I\B\h138set or move to a bookmark
	\bpos =\B\h158list bookmarks
	\bpos copy|clip\B\h098use the clipboard to store/set position
	\bpos[r] [\ix, y, z\I [\i, p, y, r \I]]\B\h020display/set (relative) position (and rotation)
	\brot[r] [\ip, y, r \I]\B\h100display/set (relative) rotation
	\bbase\B\h163display base’s nickname or previous base’s name
	\bbase \ibase \B\I\h114go to a base
	\bsystem [\isystem \I [\iobject\I | \ipos \I[, \irot\I ]]]\B
	\h173jump to a system or display current system’s nickname

	Numbers may be suffixed with \bk\B or \bK\B to multiply by 1000. Individual numbers are optional, defaulting to the current value or \b0\B, as appropriate. There are ten \
	bookmarks, \b1\B to \b9\B, with \b0\B set automatically, prior to any movement. The object, base or system is tested as a nickname first, then as a case sensitive substring of \
	the name (prefix \iobject  \Iwith \b~\B to test nickname). The object must be in the current system. \iSystem  \Imay be \b.\B for the current system; as may \ibase  \Ifor the \
	current or previous (via this command) base.\.

H 1004
	\bcspd [\ispeed \I]\B\h100display/set cruise speed
	\bcacc [\itime \I]\B\h117display/set time to reach cruise speed
	\banim [[>|<]wings|\iscript \I]\B\h020perform an animation
	\bghost\B\h164toggle collision detection
	\bgodmode\B\h134toggle invincibility
    \bdrainself\B\h139drain your shield
    \bdraintgt\B\h147drain the targeted object’s shield
    \bkillself\B\h158destroy your ship
    \bkilltgt\B\h166destroy the targeted ship

	Setting a high cruise speed may require loading a game (in order to also recognize the new maximum speed). \bCspd\B will not work with MultiCruise. The default animation \
	opens/closes the bay doors; \bwings\B is short for \bSc_extend wing\B. The first \banim\B command runs forwards, the second reverses; use \b>\B to explicitly run forwards and \b<\
	\B for backwards. \bGodmode\B takes effect on the next load.\.

H 1005
	\bntb [on|off|sight]\B\h020choose display of \un\Uon-\ut\Uargeted \ub\Urackets
	\bshow\B\h107toggles display of everything on the Nav Map
	\bshow houses\B\h044toggles display of the House labels on the Universe Map
	\bshow paths\B\h058toggles filtering of patrol paths on the Nav Map
	\bzoom [\itime \I]\B\h052display/set time to zoom Nav Map
    (\bun\B)\bmark\B\h080(un)mark the targeted object

	Sight will show the brackets when the mouse moves over the ship. Whilst bases will be shown on the Nav Map (and Contact List), it is still necessary to actually visit them to \
	obtain their info.\.

H 1006
	\bcash [[+|-]\iamount \I]\B\h034display/set (relative) amount of money
	\brep \ifaction \I[\ivalue \I]\B\h035display/set reputation with \ifaction\I
	\brep = [\ifaction \I|\ivalue\I]\B\h020set reputation for all factions
	\brep undo\B\h111restore reputation prior to first use of \b=\B
	\bships\B\h140list all your stored ships
	\bmonkey\B\h120give Trent a monkey’s head
	\brobot\B\h142turn Trent into a robot
	\btrent\B\h146restore original Trent
	\bcostume \icharacter\B\I\h035use \icharacter\I  instead of Trent

	Faction is tested as a nickname first, then as a prefix of the short name; Police factions are simply the initial of the House. \iValue\I  is a number between -1 and 1 \
	(inclusive); a percentage; or: \bH\B = -0.9; \bh\B = -0.6; \bnh\B = -0.2; \bn\B = 0; \bnf\B = 0.2; \bf\B = 0.6; & \bF\B = 0.9. Costume changes take effect on the next dock, or \
	just save & load. Female characters will not look right, due to still using the male animations.\.

H 1007
	\bcommands\B\h036list all available commands
    \bcoin\B\h089flip a coin
    \bdice\B\h089roll a dice
    \bping\B\h088measure the network latency (not really)
    \bprint/say \itext\B\I\h020output \itext\I  to the chat
	\btime\B\h089display the current time
